 "notes": "Curve taken directly from the e-print ancillary file anc/DarkPhoton_DM_Constraint_Summary_Inhomogeneous_Combined.dat (mass in eV, upper bound on kinetic mixing epsilon). This is the paper's combined Ly-alpha forest constraint (resonant + non-resonant dark-photon-to-photon conversion, 2<z<6, requiring <0.5 eV/baryon energy injection per Eq. 3.1, default sensitivity function Eq. 3.3), accounting for inhomogeneous structure; corresponds to Fig. 4. Rows saturated at epsilon=1 (unconstrained masses below ~2.2e-22 eV) removed; 401-point file downsampled with denser sampling around the resonant dip (1e-15 to 1e-9 eV). Cosmological bound assuming dark photons are all of the dark matter (Omega_CDM), independent of local DM density, so no density rescaling applied. The 0.5 eV/baryon criterion is not a formal confidence level; 0.95 entered as nominal. 21cm results in the paper are projections and excluded.",
